# Archonate

This machine runs **Archonate {{VERSION}}**: an opinionated Hyprland desktop. One
command, `archonate`, controls all of it; a Settings app and a menu (SUPER+Escape)
do the same things with a mouse. Prefer the command over editing files: it applies
changes live, keeps every app in step, and is what the user's own buttons call.

Start every task by reading the current state:

```bash
archonate status --json      # rice, style, mode, switches, the rice's settings, version
```

## The model

- **Rice**: a whole desktop (bar, fonts, corners, sounds, colours). Archonate ships
  one, `archonate`: a notch bar over a line that ripples with music, plus desktop
  widgets (visualizer, media card, clock, stats). A machine may still have older
  local rices (`archonate theme list`); they aren't part of Archonate.
- **Style**: a colour scheme with its own wallpapers, worn by the rices listed in
  `styledRices` (each remembers its own). Omarchy's dark themes, or one made from any
  image with `archonate style from <image>`.
- **Mode**: `normal`, `gaming` (bar hides over fullscreen, widgets and effects off),
  `minimal`.
- **Switches**: nightlight, dnd, caffeine, gaming, widgets, shader, screensaver,
  intros. `archonate toggle <name> [on|off]`.
- **Settings**: per rice or global, live. Change them with `archonate settings set`
  (keys below), never by editing `settings.json`.

## Doing things

| The user wants | Run |
| --- | --- |
| other colours and wallpapers | `archonate style set <style>` (list: `archonate style list`) |
| colours from a picture | `archonate style from ~/Pictures/x.jpg` |
| next wallpaper | `archonate wallpaper next` |
| gaming mode | `archonate mode set gaming` |
| desktop widgets on/off | `archonate toggle widgets on` |
| seconds on the clock | `archonate settings set barSeconds true` |
| a keybind, a layout, autostart | edit `~/.config/hypr/user.lua` (below) |
| install an app | `archonate install <packages>` (curated lists: `archonate install <section>`) |
| a website as an app | `archonate webapp new "Name" example.com` |
| a terminal program as an app | `archonate tui new "Name" "command"` |
| something looks broken | `archonate doctor`, then follow what it prints |
| updates | `archonate update` (opens a terminal; needs the user's password) |

Switching rice, style or mode changes the whole screen at once. That is fine when
the user asked for it; don't do it unprompted, and never while they are gaming or
watching something.

## Where things live

- `~/.config/hypr/`: Archonate itself (a git checkout). **Not the user's to edit and
  not yours**: updates replace it. Exceptions below.
- `~/.config/hypr/user.lua`: **the user's own file**, loaded last for every rice,
  never touched by updates. Keybinds, keyboard layouts, autostart, any Hyprland
  option. Hyprland 0.57 Lua syntax:
  ```lua
  hl.bind("SUPER + B", hl.dsp.exec_cmd("blender"))
  hl.config({ input = { kb_layout = "us,de", kb_options = "grp:win_space_toggle" } })
  hl.on("hyprland.start", function() hl.exec_cmd("nextcloud --background") end)
  ```
  Keep what is already there (layouts especially). After editing: `hyprctl reload`,
  then check `hyprctl configerrors`.
- `~/.config/archonate/hooks/<event>.d/`: the user's scripts, run after theme-set,
  mode-set, style-set, toggle, post-update, post-boot.
- `~/.local/state/hypr-rice/`: state Archonate writes (settings, switches, previews).
  Read it if useful; change it only through commands.
- **Generated, never edit by hand** (rewritten on the next switch): each rice's
  `desktop.json`, `fuzzel.ini` and `assets/wallpapers` (symlinks for styled rices),
  `active-rice.lua`, `active-mode.lua`, and the app themes Archonate writes: kitty
  `rice.conf`, GTK and Qt colours, btop, cava, Zed, Discord (`*/themes/archonate.theme.css`),
  Spotify, the Claude app theme, the zsh prompt.

## Rules

- Use `archonate ...` first; fall back to files only for `user.lua` and hooks.
- Run `archonate doctor` after any change you made by hand, and report what it says.
- No `sudo`. If a step needs root, give the user the exact command to run. Never touch
  the bootloader (limine), `/etc`, Secure Boot or snapper config.
- Don't commit, push, reset or pull in `~/.config/hypr`; updates come through
  `archonate update`.
- No light mode: every rice and style is dark on purpose.
- Keep the user's keyboard layouts and anything else they set in `user.lua`.

## Settings keys

`archonate settings set <key> <value> [--global | --rice <rice>]` (values are JSON:
`true`, `12`, `"bottom-left"`; a bare word is a string). Current values: the
`riceSettings` and `globalSettings` in `archonate status --json`.

